{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"BenevolentDM","id":"470420431841656833","is_bot":0,"username":"benevolentdm"},"author_id":"470420431841656833","channel_id":"739055105604714506","content":"Ozgur continues to work, Adze and boatwedge in hand, paying little heed to the encroaching fog hovering just above the waters surface, his Warenui is close to the woods, occasionally he stops to listen to the strange howls.","created_at":"2020-08-10T23:53:42.275000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"742531152321052693","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"BenevolentDM","id":"470420431841656833","is_bot":0,"username":"benevolentdm"},"author_id":"470420431841656833","channel_id":"739055105604714506","content":"Staggering back through the muck, Ozgur clambers onto his roof and catches his breath, refilling the birdseed beneath the sheet. After taking a short rest, he gets right back to work on the Canoes.","created_at":"2020-08-11T04:37:29.652000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"742602570316382249","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"BenevolentDM","id":"470420431841656833","is_bot":0,"username":"benevolentdm"},"author_id":"470420431841656833","channel_id":"739055105604714506","content":"Ozgur worked late into the night before eventually pulling himself up onto his roof, his tired body collapsing, falling into a dreamless slumber. He wakes up with a start, eats a handful of Nuts and berries and gets to work putting the finishing touches on the Canoes.","created_at":"2020-08-11T17:24:10.830000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-11T17:25:08.862000Z","id":"742795513241403564","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"BenevolentDM","id":"470420431841656833","is_bot":0,"username":"benevolentdm"},"author_id":"470420431841656833","channel_id":"739055105604714506","content":"Ozgur returns home to grab the birdcage with the sheet over it, and binds several sizeable logs together with thick rope, using a long tree limb to propell himself and his lumber-raft towards town. He pauses seeing his unfinished Tekoteko bobbing up and down in the water, with a sad smile he grabs it and turns to look at the carved face of his grandfather, just barely viable above the surface of the water, he smiles one last time. \"kia kite koe i a koroua.\" He then heads towards town.","created_at":"2020-08-12T00:08:12.581000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"742897190514589838","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
